scene R: The client's eyes fill as they talk about it, and {N} feels the need to get it exactly right burning in {Ns} own hands.
scene G: Shaky lines from a hand that is gone now. {N} thinks some marks should keep the tremor of the person who made them.
- W | explain honestly which lines will blur, and agree each change before inking | v: benevolence, conformity | chance: 80
- U | trace it, keep every quirk, and redraw only what the needle cannot hold | v: achievement | chance: 78
- B | redraw it in your own style; your name goes on the work | v: power, achievement | identity | chance: 45
- R | draw it straight onto the skin with a marker, together, until it feels right | v: self-direction, stimulation | chance: 78
- G | tattoo it exactly as drawn, wobbles and all | v: tradition, benevolence | identity | chance: 70
- W>R | book a second session just to try the stencil on and live with it a week | v: self-direction | chance: 80
- U>G | ask to see more of the father's drawings, and learn his hand | v: benevolence, tradition | chance: 75
- B>W | refuse to ink it as it is; your studio does not put out work that blurs | v: power, conformity | chance: 65
- R>U | stay after closing and draw twenty versions until one is right | v: achievement | habit | self_control: + | chance: 78
- G>B | do it with care, then ask if you can share it, with the story, online | v: achievement | tech: internet | chance: 72
works: The client looks in the mirror for a long time, then hugs {N} without a word.
