scene U: {N} notices the ache is worst after shading, and starts thinking about grips, angles and the weight of the machine.
scene B: The diary is full because {N} is the best in town right now. Every cancelled session is money, and a client who might go elsewhere.
scene R: {N} loves the buzz of the machine more than anything, and the thought of putting it down even for a month is unbearable.
scene G: The body has been giving its signal for months. {N} has heard old artists talk about hands that simply stopped one day.
- W | see a doctor, and follow whatever rest they prescribe | v: security, conformity | chance: 70
- U | switch to a lighter machine and a new grip, and track the ache for a month | v: achievement | mark: learned a skill | chance: 72
- B | hire a junior for the simple pieces, and keep the big work for yourself | v: achievement, power | chance: 85
- R | cancel a month of bookings at once and go travelling until the hand heals | v: stimulation, hedonism | door | chance: 82
- G | cut down to four days a week, and let the hand set the pace | v: security | self_control: + | chance: 75
- W>G | set yourself a firm rule: no session over four hours, ever | v: security | habit | chance: 65
- U>W | write a safe-working guide for the studio, so the juniors are spared it | v: benevolence | chance: 90
- B>U | pay for sessions with a hand physiotherapist who treats musicians | v: achievement, security | chance: 85
- R>B | teach a weekend workshop, and earn from your name instead of your wrist | v: achievement | chance: 70
- G>R | take the slower weeks as a gift, and draw just for the pleasure of it | v: hedonism | chance: 90
