- U>B | rewrite it so it seems to do what they asked, and keep what matters | v: achievement, power | chance: 60
- B>R | get an agent to shop the book around, so you can afford to say no | v: self-direction | door | chance: 20
- R>G | take the manuscript back to the town it is set in, and read the ending there | v: self-direction, tradition | chance: 80
- G>W | let your writing group read both versions, and go with what they agree | v: conformity | chance: 65
works: The book goes to press with an ending {N} can read aloud without flinching.
works: The editor reads the new pages and writes back one line: this is it.
fails: The publisher withdraws the offer, politely, by email on a Friday afternoon.
fails: The book comes out with the new ending, and {N} cannot bear to read the last chapter at events.

